From 4f685980cd4f6ffb05756ca132c182f621dbfbdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mariuslozo-boop <254631011+mariuslozo-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 06:37:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/33] DirectStorage: refuse unpaged buffers over 32 MiB,
 count stats at submit, /EHa under clang-cl

Review fixes for #4348 (Flyander, AirKyzzZ):
- DSTORAGE_REQUEST allows a buffer over 32 MiB only with 64 KiB or 2 MiB
  pages, which are not implemented yet, so such a request now fails with
  E_DSTORAGE_REQUEST_TOO_LARGE before any memory is touched.
- TotalRequestCount and the byte totals grow when a request is submitted,
  not when it is enqueued, and PendingRequestCount counts the request the
  worker is processing (DSTORAGE_PRIORITY_STATS).
- dstorage.cpp is built with /EHa under clang-cl, so guarded_move's __try
  catches an access violation in a title's buffer there too.

Tests: an over-limit and an at-limit 32 MiB copy, and stats checked
before Submit and while a copy is held on a guard page. The three new
failing checks fail with the previous shim.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
